# BassScore runs with NO API KEYS by default.
# Copy to `.env` only if you want to change the tide source.
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables into the JS bundle at build time, so
# anything here is readable by anyone who has the app. Never put a secret in it.

# Optional. Enables the WorldTides provider (station-grade tide predictions).
# Free tier: https://www.worldtides.info/developer
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WORLDTIDES_API_KEY=

# Optional. Force a provider instead of letting the registry choose.
# One of: open-meteo | worldtides
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TIDE_PROVIDER=open-meteo

# Optional. Google Analytics 4 measurement id for pecheaubar.fr.
#
# Read by `scripts/build-site.mjs`, not by the app, so it is a plain build
# variable rather than an EXPO_PUBLIC_ one — and it is NOT loaded from this
# file. Set it in the host (Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables), or
# inline for a one-off local build:
#
#   GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX npm run build:web
#
# Left unset, the site builds with no analytics at all — which is what you
# want for local and preview builds.
# GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
